<div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 py-8 text-gray-900 dark:text-gray-100">
  <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-gray-900 dark:text-white mb-3">
    Files on Bitcoin
  </h1>
  <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-2 max-w-3xl">
    Every B:// file in the blocks Bitblocks stores, newest first.
    Each one is read from its transaction as this page loads.
  </p>
  <.freshness
    id="files-freshness"
    class="mb-2 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 max-w-3xl"
    through={@freshness.through}
    tip={@freshness.tip}
  />
  <p class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-6 max-w-3xl">
    B:// is the file protocol unwriter published in 2019: a file's bytes, media type and name in one transaction output.
    A file's C:// address is the sha256 of its bytes, so every copy of the same file shares it.
    Files open at
    <code class="font-mono">/b/&lt;txid&gt;</code>
    by transaction, or at
    <code class="font-mono">/c/&lt;sha256&gt;</code>
    by C:// address, as untrusted content, with scripts switched off.
    A file opened by its C:// address is hashed again before it is served.
  </p>

  <form
    id="files-search"
    action={~p"/files"}
    method="get"
    phx-submit="search"
    role="search"
    aria-label="Find a file"
    class="mb-6 rounded-lg border p-4 bg-gray-50 border-gray-200 dark:bg-gray-800 dark:border-gray-700"
  >
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3 sm:flex-row sm:items-end">
      <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
        <label
          for="files-q"
          class="block text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-1"
        >
          Find a file
        </label>
        <input
          id="files-q"
          type="search"
          name="q"
          value={@q}
          maxlength={@max_query}
          placeholder="Part of a name, or a C:// address"
          autocomplete="off"
          class="block w-full rounded border px-3 py-2 text-sm bg-white border-gray-300 text-gray-900 dark:bg-gray-800 dark:border-gray-600 dark:text-gray-100"
        />
      </div>
      <div>
        <label
          for="files-type"
          class="block text-sm font-medium text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 mb-1"
        >
          Type
        </label>
        <select
          id="files-type"
          name="type"
          class="block w-full sm:w-auto rounded border px-3 py-2 text-sm bg-white border-gray-300 text-gray-900 dark:bg-gray-800 dark:border-gray-600 dark:text-gray-100"
        >
          <option
            :for={{label, value} <- @type_options}
            value={value}
            selected={(@type || "") == value}
          >
            {label}
          </option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <button
        type="submit"
        class="rounded px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium bg-blue-600 text-white hover:bg-blue-700"
      >
        Search
      </button>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400">
      Searches the C:// index of B:// and BCat files by name and type.
      A C:// address (64 hex characters) opens that file.
    </p>
  </form>

  <section
    :if={@mode == :search}
    id="files-search-results"
    aria-label="Search results"
  >
    <div
      id="files-coverage"
      class="mb-4 text-sm text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 max-w-3xl"
    >
      <%= cond do %>
        <% @coverage.indexed_through_height -> %>
          <.freshness
            id="files-index-freshness"
            class=""
            label="Files indexed through"
            through={@coverage.indexed_through_height}
            tip={@freshness.tip}
          />
          Searching the C:// index of B:// and BCat files from block 0.
          Later blocks join it as the sync stores them.
        <% @coverage.earliest_indexed_height -> %>
          Searching the C:// index, which holds files from block {delimit(
            @coverage.earliest_indexed_height
          )} on, until its backfill covers block 0.
          A file in an older block may be on chain and not found here.
        <% true -> %>
          The C:// index holds no files yet, until its backfill covers block 0.
          A file may be on chain and not found here.
      <% end %>
      <%= case @coverage.bcat_unassembled do %>
        <% 0 -> %>
        <% 1 -> %>
          One BCat file we know of couldn't be assembled from its chunks, so it isn't in the index.
        <% n -> %>
          {delimit(n)} BCat files we know of couldn't be assembled from their chunks, so they aren't in the index.
      <% end %>
    </div>

    <div
      :if={@search_error}
      id="files-search-error"
      role="alert"
      class="mb-6 rounded-lg border p-4 bg-red-50 border-red-200 text-red-800 dark:bg-red-900/30 dark:border-red-800 dark:text-red-200"
    >
      The search couldn't finish just now.
      Try again in a minute, or narrow it.
    </div>

    <div
      :if={@address}
      id="files-address-miss"
      class="mb-6 rounded-lg border p-4 bg-white border-gray-200 text-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-800 dark:border-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200"
    >
      <p class="break-all">
        No file in the C:// index has the address
        <code class="font-mono">c://{@address}</code>.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-1">
        That is a miss in our index, not proof the file doesn't exist.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div
      :if={@results == [] and is_nil(@search_error) and is_nil(@address)}
      id="files-no-match"
      class="mb-6 rounded-lg border p-4 bg-white border-gray-200 text-gray-800 dark:bg-gray-800 dark:border-gray-700 dark:text-gray-200"
    >
      <p class="break-all">
        <%= if @first_page do %>
          No indexed file matches{if @q, do: " “#{@q}”"}{if @type,
            do: " of type #{type_label(@type)}"}.
        <% else %>
          No more indexed files match.
        <% end %>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-1">
        That is a miss in our index, not proof the file doesn't exist.
        Try part of the name, or another type.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div
      :if={@results != []}
      class="overflow-x-auto bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg dark:bg-gray-800 dark:border-gray-700"
    >
      <table
        id="files-results"
        class="min-w-full text-sm"
      >
        <thead class="bg-gray-50 text-left text-gray-700 dark:bg-gray-900 dark:text-gray-300">
          <tr>
            <th class="px-4 py-2">
              File
            </th>
            <th class="px-4 py-2">
              Type
            </th>
            <th class="px-4 py-2 text-right">
              Size
            </th>
            <th class="px-4 py-2 text-right">
              Block
            </th>
            <th class="px-4 py-2">
              C:// address
            </th>
            <th class="px-4 py-2">
              Transaction
            </th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr
            :for={file <- @results}
            id={"result-#{file.id}"}
            class="border-t border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700"
          >
            <td class="px-4 py-2 break-all">
              <a
                href={open_path(file)}
                class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
              >
                {file.filename || "untitled"}
              </a>
            </td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              {file.media_type || "unstated"}
              <span
                :if={file.kind == "bcat"}
                class="block font-sans text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400"
              >
                BCat, {file.chunks} chunks
              </span>
            </td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2 text-right font-mono tabular-nums text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              {delimit(file.size)} B
            </td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2 text-right font-mono tabular-nums text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              {if file.block_height, do: delimit(file.block_height), else: "unknown"}
            </td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">
              <a
                href={~p"/c/#{hex(file.sha256)}"}
                title={"c://#{hex(file.sha256)}"}
                class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
              >
                c://{short(hex(file.sha256))}
              </a>
            </td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">
              <.link
                navigate={~p"/transactions/#{file.txid}"}
                class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
              >
                {short(file.txid)}
              </.link>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <nav
      class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-6 text-sm"
      aria-label="Pages of search results"
    >
      <.link
        id="files-clear"
        patch={~p"/files"}
        class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
      >
        Clear search
      </.link>
      <.link
        :if={not @first_page}
        patch={~p"/files?#{next_query(@q, @type, nil)}"}
        class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
      >
        First results
      </.link>
      <.link
        :if={@next_cursor}
        id="files-more"
        patch={~p"/files?#{next_query(@q, @type, @next_cursor)}"}
        class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
      >
        More results
      </.link>
    </nav>
  </section>

  <section
    :if={@mode == :list}
    id="files-list"
    aria-label="Newest files"
  >
    <div
      :if={@error}
      id="files-error"
      role="alert"
      class="mb-6 rounded-lg border p-4 bg-red-50 border-red-200 text-red-800 dark:bg-red-900/30 dark:border-red-800 dark:text-red-200"
    >
      The file list couldn't be read just now.
      Try again in a minute.
    </div>

    <p
      :if={@files == [] and is_nil(@error)}
      id="files-empty"
      class="text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300"
    >
      No B:// files in the stored blocks yet.
    </p>

    <div
      :if={@files != []}
      class="overflow-x-auto bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-lg dark:bg-gray-800 dark:border-gray-700"
    >
      <table
        id="files"
        class="min-w-full text-sm"
      >
        <thead class="bg-gray-50 text-left text-gray-700 dark:bg-gray-900 dark:text-gray-300">
          <tr>
            <th class="px-4 py-2">
              File
            </th>
            <th class="px-4 py-2">
              Type
            </th>
            <th class="px-4 py-2 text-right">
              Size
            </th>
            <th class="px-4 py-2 text-right">
              Block
            </th>
            <th class="px-4 py-2">
              C:// address
            </th>
            <th class="px-4 py-2">
              Transaction
            </th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr
            :for={file <- @files}
            id={"file-#{file.txid}"}
            class="border-t border-gray-100 dark:border-gray-700"
          >
            <%= if file.parsed do %>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 break-all">
                <a
                  href={~p"/b/#{file.txid}"}
                  class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
                >
                  {file.filename || "untitled"}
                </a>
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                {file.media_type || "unstated"}
              </td>
              <td class="px-4 py-2 text-right font-mono tabular-nums text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
                {delimit(file.size)} B
              </td>
            <% else %>
              <td
                colspan="3"
                class="px-4 py-2 text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400"
              >
                No B:// file could be read from this transaction.
              </td>
            <% end %>
            <td class="px-4 py-2 text-right font-mono tabular-nums text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300">
              {if file.block_height, do: delimit(file.block_height), else: "unconfirmed"}
            </td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">
              <a
                :if={file.sha256}
                href={~p"/c/#{file.sha256}"}
                title={"c://#{file.sha256}"}
                class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
              >
                c://{short(file.sha256)}
              </a>
            </td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2 font-mono text-xs">
              <.link
                navigate={~p"/transactions/#{file.txid}"}
                class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
              >
                {short(file.txid)}
              </.link>
            </td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <nav
      :if={@next || not @first_page}
      class="mt-4 flex gap-6 text-sm"
      aria-label="Pages of files"
    >
      <.link
        :if={not @first_page}
        navigate={~p"/files"}
        class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
      >
        Newest files
      </.link>
      <.link
        :if={@next}
        id="files-older"
        navigate={~p"/files?#{[before: @next]}"}
        class="text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
      >
        Older files
      </.link>
    </nav>
  </section>

  <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-gray-600 dark:text-gray-400 max-w-3xl">
    The list grows as the sync stores more blocks.
    B:// and C:// are unwriter's conventions; this is an independent reading of them from the chain.
    For a namespace's own files and routes, see the
    <.link
      navigate={~p"/bitcom"}
      class="underline text-blue-700 hover:text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-400 dark:hover:text-blue-300"
    >
      Bitcom registry
    </.link>.
  </p>
</div>
